SUMMARY:CANCELLED: Psychosocial Research Rounds - Social media use and perinatal mental health: A...
LOCATION:ICFP Amphitheatre, 4333 Côte-Ste-Catherine Rd., Montreal QC H3T 1E4
DESCRIPTION:This round has been cancelled.\n\nSocial media use and perinatal mental health: A scoping review\n\nSpeaker: Lucia Shi\nChair: Vincent Paquin\nFormat: Hybrid\n\nLearning Objectives:\n•	Describe the current evidence on the relationship between social media use and parental mental health during the perinatal period, including both positive and negative effects.\n•	Identify how characteristics of social media use (e.g., platform, frequency, type of engagement, and purpose of use) are associated with mental health outcomes such as depression, anxiety, and psychological distress in perinatal populations.\n•	Recognize gaps in the existing literature regarding social media use and perinatal mental health to inform future research and clinical practice.\n\nZoom: https://us06web.zoom.us/j/88488947071?pwd=SfbahYa0VEe7nCL2Hbc1aA6bXzfZeR.1
URL:https://us06web.zoom.us/j/88488947071?pwd=SfbahYa0VEe7nCL2Hbc1aA6bXzfZeR.1
END:VEVENT

