SUMMARY:Psychosocial Research Rounds - Canadian news media coverage of AI chatbots in ...
LOCATION:ICFP Amphitheatre, 4333 Côte-Ste-Catherine Rd., Montreal QC H3T 1E4
DESCRIPTION:Canadian news media coverage of AI chatbots in mental health care: A framing analysis of risks, benefits, and agency distribution\n\nSpeaker: Édouard Coulombe\nChair: Vincent Paquin\nFormat: Hybrid\n\nLearning Objectives:\n•	Explain why news media analysis is relevant to understanding public perceptions and the potential adoption of AI chatbots in mental health care.\n•	Describe how a media framing approach can be used to examine representations of risks, benefits, and the distribution of agency between AI systems, clinicians, and other stakeholders.\n•	Reflect on potential risks and benefits of using AI chatbots in mental health care.\n\nZoom: https://us06web.zoom.us/j/88488947071?pwd=SfbahYa0VEe7nCL2Hbc1aA6bXzfZeR.1
URL:https://us06web.zoom.us/j/88488947071?pwd=SfbahYa0VEe7nCL2Hbc1aA6bXzfZeR.1
