SUMMARY:Psychosocial Research Rounds - Prevalence of common parasomnias and their asso...
LOCATION:ICFP Amphitheatre, 4333 Côte-Ste-Catherine Rd., Montreal QC H3T 1E4
DESCRIPTION:Prevalence of common parasomnias and their associations with sleep quality, insomnia, anxiety, and depression among post-secondary students and young adults\n\nSpeaker: Samantha Groppini\nChair: Vincent Paquin\nFormat: Hybrid\n\nLearning Objectives:\n•	Describe the prevalence of common parasomnias among post-secondary students and young adults.\n•	Examine the associations between common parasomnias and sleep quality, insomnia, anxiety, and depression in this population.\n•	Discuss how the findings of this systematic review may inform future research, clinical practice, and sleep health initiatives for post-secondary students and young adults.\n\nZoom: https://us06web.zoom.us/j/88488947071?pwd=SfbahYa0VEe7nCL2Hbc1aA6bXzfZeR.1
URL:https://us06web.zoom.us/j/88488947071?pwd=SfbahYa0VEe7nCL2Hbc1aA6bXzfZeR.1
