SUMMARY:Psychosocial Research Rounds - Improving sleep health in post-secondary studen...
LOCATION:ICFP Amphitheatre, 4333 Côte-Ste-Catherine Rd., Montreal QC H3T 1E4
DESCRIPTION:Improving sleep health in post-secondary students: Evidence-based coping strategies and knowledge translation tools\n\nSpeaker: Noemi Di Pietrantonio\nChair: Vincent Paquin\nFormat: Hybrid\n\nLearning Objectives:\n•	To synthesize the current evidence on interventions for common parasomnias and sleep-related disorders and translate this evidence into accessible, evidence-informed resources for young adults and healthcare professionals.\n•	To bridge the gap between research evidence and practical sleep health resources for post-secondary students.\n•	To identify evidence-based behavioural, psychological, pharmacological, and educational interventions for common parasomnias.\n\nZoom: https://us06web.zoom.us/j/88488947071?pwd=SfbahYa0VEe7nCL2Hbc1aA6bXzfZeR.1
URL:https://us06web.zoom.us/j/88488947071?pwd=SfbahYa0VEe7nCL2Hbc1aA6bXzfZeR.1
